  "cut_point": "We are given a **best-of-seven** NBA Finals series between the **Los Angeles Lakers** and the **Boston Celtics**. The series is played in a **best-of-seven** format, meaning the **first team to win 4 games** is crowned champion.\n\n### Step 1: Understand the structure of the series\n- The **first 2 games** are played in **Los Angeles** (games 1 and 2).\n- The **next 3 games** (games 3, 4, 5) are played in **Boston**.\n- The **7th game** is played in **Los Angeles** if needed (i.e., if the series is tied 3-3 after 6 games).\n\nSo the **home games** are:\n- **Games 1, 2, 6, 7** → **Los Angeles**\n- **Games 3, 4, 5** → **Boston**\n\nBut the **Lakers win the series on their home court**, which means that the **series ends in Game 7**, and **Game 7 is played in LA**.",
